# Example Caddyfile for a self-hosted deploy fronted by Caddy.
# Caddy handles TLS automatically (via Let's Encrypt) and proxies both
# normal HTTP requests and WebSocket upgrades to the Node process,
# no special WebSocket configuration needed. Caddy detects the Upgrade
# header itself.
#
# Copy this to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or your platform's equivalent),
# replace the domain, and reload Caddy.

pear.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
